    "rich_text_6aeaLY": {
      "type": "rich_text",
      "name": "Rich Text",
      "settings": {
        "richtext_inhalt": "<h3></h3><h3>SEGMENT 1: EDUCATION</h3><p><strong>DIGITALISATION IN EDUCATION – STRUCTURAL TAILWIND</strong></p><p>The Digital Pact for Schools (Germany), the ‘Bildung.digital’ initiative (Switzerland) and similar programmes in other European countries have mobilised billions for the digitalisation of schools. Tablets and laptops for pupils are no longer the exception, but the norm. And with every device comes the need for robust, pupil-friendly accessories.<br/>Schools do not buy just one device – they buy 200, 500 or 2,000 devices at a time. And they need cases that are truly robust: children’s school bags are not a gentle environment. DICOTA offers products designed for the education sector – hard-wearing, easy to clean and available in a range of colours.</p><p><strong><br/>THE SCHOOL AUTHORITY AS THE KEY DECISION-MAKER</strong></p><p>In Germany and Switzerland, it is not the individual school that makes the purchase, but the school authority – that is, the local council, district or canton. This means: one decision-maker for many schools. Whoever wins over the school authority doesn’t just secure one contract, but potentially twenty.<br/>The best way to get started is via the relevant IT manager at the school authority – often a digitalisation department or an IT centre. The pitch: “We don’t just supply the devices, but the complete, documented setup including protective accessories – everything from a single source, all compliant with tender specifications.”</p><h3><br/>SEGMENT 2: PUBLIC SECTOR / GOVERNMENT AGENCIES</h3><p><strong>FRAMEWORK AGREEMENTS: THE KEY TO PREDICTABILITY</strong></p><p>Government agencies procure goods and services via framework agreements, which typically run for 3 to 5 years. During this period, products can be ordered on demand – without having to put the contract out to tender each time. For resellers, this is a goldmine: once a framework agreement has been secured, it means predictable turnover for years to come.</p><p>DICOTA supports resellers in preparing bids for framework agreements – with comprehensive product documentation, price transparency and clearly defined delivery terms. This reduces the workload for resellers and enhances the quality of their bids.</p><p><strong><br/>UNDERSTANDING AND MEETING COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS</strong></p><p>Public sector clients have strict requirements for their suppliers: CE marking, RoHS compliance, data protection compliance, proof of origin, sustainability certificates. These requirements are not obstacles – they are qualification criteria. Resellers who can provide this evidence qualify; all others are excluded.</p><p>DICOTA makes all relevant certificates and evidence available digitally – accessible, up-to-date and ready for immediate use in tender documents. For resellers, this means: no time spent on research, no waiting for documents, and no gaps in the documentation.<br/><br/></p>",
        "width": "narrow",
        "padding_top": 4,
        "padding_bottom": 4
      }
    },
